    "summary": "Joined Miles Davis at seventeen and remade jazz time in the Second Great Quintet: a ride so light it nearly straightens at speed, rimshot stabs, bombs and broken time, and phrases in three running across the bar line, so the drums became a full voice in the band's improvising. Then led Lifetime, the loud organ trio with John McLaughlin and Larry Young that helped start jazz-rock."
